module

public import Sheaf.CategoryTheory.Sites.GeometricMorphism
public import Sheaf.CategoryTheory.Sites.GrothendieckTopos
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Over
import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Limits

/-!
# Explicit adjunction for localization on a finite-limit site

Source: Stacks Project, Sites, Tags 03CE and 00Y2
(blueprint: lem-trf-slice-subtopos-site-presentation).

The localized topology is Mathlib's `GrothendieckTopology.over`. Inverse image is
`GrothendieckTopology.overPullback`: it evaluates a sheaf at the underlying object of
the slice and leaves restrictions unchanged. The direct-image object and morphism
formulas specify precomposition with `V ↦ V × U → U` and `q ↦ q × 1`.
Mathlib's `Over.star U` uses the opposite product order, so the formulas below
explicitly retain the product order of the source.
The coefficient universe contains the universe of the small site, as in
`def-weil-pbc-topos` and the project's size convention.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- The restriction and product-precomposition functors give the localization geometric
morphism, with counit restriction along the graph. Source: Stacks Project, Sites,
Tag 03CE, especially (3), and Tag 00Y2
(blueprint: lem-trf-slice-subtopos-site-presentation).

Proof:
1. Take all small families whose generated sieve is covering. Maximality, pullback
stability, and transitivity give the covering-family site axioms of
`def-weil-pbc-sites-and-cohomology`. The family and sieve sheaf conditions agree:
extend a compatible family to its generated sieve using restrictions; independence
of factorization follows by comparing on pairwise fibre products. Conversely restrict
a sieve matching family to its generators. Every covering sieve is generated by its
own arrows, so this treats every cover (Stacks 00ZC).
2. The slice is small and its coverings are the underlying coverings. Its fibre products
are the underlying fibre products equipped with their common arrow to `U`. The sheaf
condition for restriction is therefore exactly the original sheaf condition. Restricting
natural transformations gives the inverse-image functor (Stacks 00Y0).
3. Products give the functor `V ↦ V × U → U`. Pullback stability makes the families
`Vᵢ × U → V × U` covering, and their pairwise fibre products are
`(Vᵢ ×[V] Vⱼ) × U`. Thus precomposition takes sheaves to sheaves, with restrictions
and natural transformations given by precomposition (Stacks 03CE).
4. For `a : RA ⟶ G`, define its transpose at `V` by first restricting `A` along
`pr₁ : V × U → V` and then applying `a` at `V × U → U`. Naturality follows from
`pr₁ ∘ (q × 1) = q ∘ pr₁`; this gives a morphism `A ⟶ HG`.
5. Conversely, from `b : A ⟶ HG` define the component at `t : W → U` by `b_W`
followed by restriction along the graph `(1_W,t)`. The graph identity for a map over
`U` proves naturality. Both constructions commute with pre- and postcomposition.
6. The two round trips are identities: use `pr₁ ∘ (1_W,t) = 1_W` for one and
`(pr₁ × 1) ∘ (1,pr₂) = 1` for the other, together with naturality. These natural
inverse Hom maps give the adjunction; transposing the identity gives exactly the
counit in the conclusion.
7. Limits of sheaves are computed sectionwise by
`lem-weil-pbc-site-sheaf-sets-limits-sectionwise`. Restriction evaluates both limit
cones at the same underlying object, so it preserves every finite limit, including
the terminal object. The small-site presentations give topoi in the sense of
`def-weil-pbc-topos`; the adjunction and left exactness give the geometric-morphism
datum `def-trf-geometric-morphism`. -/
theorem slice_subtopos_site_presentation
    {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] [HasFiniteLimits C]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (U : C) :
    ∃ j : GeometricMorphism (Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w)))
        (Sheaf J (Type (max u w))),
      j.inverse = J.overPullback (Type (max u w)) U ∧
      (∀ (G : Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) (V : C),
        (j.direct.obj G).obj.obj (op V) =
          G.obj.obj (op (Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod V U ⟶ U)))) ∧
      (∀ (G : Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) (V V' : C) (q : V' ⟶ V),
        HEq ((j.direct.obj G).obj.map q.op)
          (G.obj.map (Over.homMk
            (U := Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod V' U ⟶ U))
            (V := Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod V U ⟶ U))
            (Limits.prod.map q (𝟙 U))).op)) ∧
      (∀ (G G' : Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) (f : G ⟶ G') (V : C),
        HEq ((j.direct.map f).hom.app (op V))
          (f.hom.app (op (Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod V U ⟶ U))))) ∧
      ∀ (G : Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) (W : C) (t : W ⟶ U),
        HEq ((j.adj.counit.app G).hom.app (op (Over.mk t)))
          (G.obj.map (Over.homMk (U := Over.mk t)
            (V := Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod W U ⟶ U))
            (Limits.prod.lift (𝟙 W) t)).op) := by
  let v : C ⥤ Over U :=
    { obj := fun V ↦ Over.mk (Limits.prod.snd : Limits.prod V U ⟶ U)
      map := fun q ↦ Over.homMk (Limits.prod.map q (𝟙 U))
      map_id := by intro V; ext; simp
      map_comp := by intro V V' V'' q r; ext; simp }
  let adj : Over.forget U ⊣ v :=
    { unit :=
        { app := fun W ↦ Over.homMk (Limits.prod.lift (𝟙 W.left) W.hom)
          naturality := by intro W W' q; ext; simp [v, Over.w q] }
      counit :=
        { app := fun V ↦ Limits.prod.fst
          naturality := by intro V V' q; simp [v] }
      left_triangle_components := by intro W; simp
      right_triangle_components := by intro V; ext; simp [v] }
  let : v.IsContinuous J (J.over U) :=
    adj.isContinuous_of_isCocontinuous (J.over U) J
  let j : GeometricMorphism (Sheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w)))
      (Sheaf J (Type (max u w))) :=
    { inverse := J.overPullback (Type (max u w)) U
      direct := v.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (max u w)) J (J.over U)
      adj := adj.sheafPushforwardContinuous (E := Type (max u w)) (J.over U) J
      leftExact := by
        have : PreservesFiniteLimits
            (J.overPullback (Type (max u w)) U ⋙
              sheafToPresheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) := by
          change PreservesFiniteLimits
            (sheafToPresheaf J (Type (max u w)) ⋙
              (Functor.whiskeringLeft (Over U)ᵒᵖ Cᵒᵖ (Type (max u w))).obj (Over.forget U).op)
          infer_instance
        exact preservesFiniteLimits_of_reflects_of_preserves _
          (sheafToPresheaf (J.over U) (Type (max u w))) }
  refine ⟨j, rfl, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro G V; rfl
  · intro G V V' q; rfl
  · intro G G' f V; rfl
  · intro G W t; rfl

end CategoryTheory
